//? Title: Buddy Allocation: Splitting, Rounding and True Buddies
//? Subtitle: Actual native allocation paths, owned arena snapshots and the limits of coalescing
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A binary buddy system manages a power-of-two arena by splitting blocks and
coalescing free siblings. We preserve the original 1024-byte arena, 32-byte
minimum, and requests of 30, 100 and 50 bytes. Actual native traces show how
their offsets and rounding waste arise. A second example leaves enough free
bytes for a request that still fails: adjacent free blocks need not be buddies.
The C++ class models byte offsets and allocation metadata, without allocating
payload storage. Checked dimensions and requests avoid invalid shifts; owned
snapshots and operation traces make its invariants inspectable.
)

\toc

> First split path: reserve 32 bytes for a 30-byte request

An arena of size T and minimum block m has orders zero through h, where
T=m*2^h. An order-k block has size B_k=m*2^k and an offset divisible by B_k.
The allocator selects the smallest adequate order containing a free block,
then the lowest offset in that order. If necessary it repeatedly halves that
block, retaining the left child and placing its right buddy in a free set.

For the original T=1024, m=32 arena, the first 30-byte request needs order
zero. There is initially only one order-five block. The actual path contains
five splits, leaving one free buddy at each smaller order. Reserving 32 bytes
for the request leaves two bytes unused inside the allocated block.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/buddy_allocator_split.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::algorithms::BuddyAllocator arena(1024,32);
  const auto trace=arena.allocate_trace(30);
  const auto state=arena.snapshot();
  if (trace.offset!=0 || trace.splits.size()!=5 || state.internal_fragmentation!=2) return 1;
  std::print("| parent offset | parent order | parent bytes | retained left child | free right buddy | child bytes |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  std::string free_buddies="remaining free buddies";
  for (const auto& step:trace.splits) {
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",step.offset,step.parent_order,
        arena.block_size(step.parent_order),step.offset,step.offset+step.half_size,step.half_size);
    free_buddies+=std::format("\noffset {}: {} B",step.offset+step.half_size,step.half_size);
  }
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram(65,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;style.width=3.5;style.height=1.8;
  diagram.node("whole",{0,0},"initial free block\noffset 0, 1024 B",style)
      .node("split",{5,0},std::format("{} actual splits\nretain each left child",trace.splits.size()),style);
  style.fill={220,252,231};
  diagram.node("allocated",{10,0},std::format("allocated at {}\n32 B reserved, {} B used",trace.offset,trace.requested),style);
  style.fill={239,246,255};style.height=3.7;style.width=4;
  diagram.node("free",{5,-4},free_buddies,style)
      .edge("whole","split").edge("split","allocated").edge("split","free")
      .text({0,-4},"offsets are relative\nto logical arena zero")
      .text({10,-4},std::format("{} free bytes\n{} B internal waste",state.free_bytes,state.internal_fragmentation))
      .save_svg("build/buddy_allocator_split.svg");
  std::print("\nFree-list orders examined: {}; actual returned offset: {}.\n",trace.orders_examined,trace.offset);
  std::print("Actual free offsets by order: {}.\n",state.free_offsets);
}
```
