\caption(The path and buddy addresses come directly from the allocation kernel. The split node groups five actual steps; its table retains every parent and child size.)
\alttext(A free 1024-byte block undergoes five splits. A 32-byte block at offset zero serves the 30-byte request. Remaining free buddies occupy offsets 512, 256, 128, 64 and 32 with the corresponding byte sizes.)

No backing byte buffer is created by BuddyAllocator. Offsets describe a logical
arena, so this class demonstrates allocation policy rather than replacing malloc.
The maps and free sets themselves do allocate host metadata. Copies model
independent arenas; snapshots own their records and remain valid after mutation.

> The original three requests and complete coalescence

Retain requests A=30, B=100 and C=50 bytes, allocated in that order. They
reserve blocks of 32, 128 and 64 bytes at offsets 0, 128 and 64. This is
smallest-available-order selection, rather than globally choosing the lowest
address that could be obtained by splitting any larger block.

The native snapshot records both the reserved bytes and the actual requests.
The original free-count histogram is retained. After freeing A, B and C in
that order, their buddy cascades restore exactly one full-arena free block.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/buddy_allocator.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::algorithms::BuddyAllocator arena(1024,32);
  const std::vector<int> requests{30,100,50};
  const std::vector<std::string> names{"A","B","C"};
  std::vector<int> offsets;
  std::print("| allocation | requested bytes | offset | reserved block bytes | actual splits |\n"
             "| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (std::size_t i=0;i<requests.size();++i) {
    const auto t=arena.allocate_trace(requests[i]);
    if (t.offset<0) return 1;
    offsets.push_back(t.offset);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",names[i],requests[i],t.offset,arena.block_size(t.desired_order),t.splits.size());
  }
  const auto before=arena.snapshot();
  const auto counts=arena.free_blocks_per_order();
  if (offsets!=std::vector<int>{0,128,64} || before.allocated_bytes!=224 || before.requested_bytes!=180) return 1;
  std::print("\nReserved: {} B; requested: {} B; internal waste: {} B ({:.2f}% of reserved bytes).\n",
      before.allocated_bytes,before.requested_bytes,before.internal_fragmentation,
      100.0*before.internal_fragmentation/before.allocated_bytes);
  std::print("Free counts after allocation: {}. Total free bytes: {}.\n\n",counts,before.free_bytes);
  std::print("| free | successful merges | actual probes | resulting offset | resulting order | free counts after release |\n"
             "| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for (std::size_t i=0;i<offsets.size();++i) {
    const auto t=arena.free_trace(offsets[i]);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",names[i],t.merges,t.probes.size(),t.final_offset,t.final_order,arena.free_blocks_per_order());
  }
  const auto after=arena.snapshot();
  if (after.blocks.size()!=1 || after.blocks[0].allocated || after.largest_free_block!=1024) return 1;
  std::vector<double> heights;std::vector<std::string> labels;
  for (std::size_t order=0;order<counts.size();++order) {
    heights.push_back(counts[order]);labels.push_back(std::format("{} B",arena.block_size(static_cast<int>(order))));
  }
  dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(heights,labels,"free blocks after A, B, C",dm::RGB{37,99,235})
      .title("Original mid-run free-block counts")
      .x_label("block size (bytes)").y_label("number of free blocks").size(1000,480)
      .save_svg("build/buddy_allocator.svg");
  std::print("\nFinal largest free block: {} B; allocated bytes: {}. Earlier owned snapshot still records {} reserved bytes.\n",
      after.largest_free_block,after.allocated_bytes,before.allocated_bytes);
}
```
