\image(figures/buddy_allocator.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The original free counts [1,0,0,1,1,0] describe one 32-byte block, one 256-byte block and one 512-byte block: 800 free bytes in total. Counts are numbers of blocks, not bytes.)
\alttext(A bar chart indexed by block sizes 32, 64, 128, 256, 512 and 1024 bytes has height one at 32, 256 and 512, and height zero at the other sizes.)

For a current offset a and block size B, the unique same-order buddy is

\[
\operatorname{buddy}(a,B)=a\mathbin{\mathrm{XOR}}B.
\]

Because a is aligned to B and m is a power of two, flipping that bit selects
the other half of the same aligned 2B-byte parent. If that buddy appears in
the actual free set at the same order, the two blocks merge at their smaller
offset. Each merge increases the order, so the process terminates at the
arena's maximum order or at the first unavailable buddy. Eager coalescing
maintains the invariant that no two free same-order buddies remain separate.

The original rounding waste is 224-minus-180=44 bytes, or 19.64% of reserved
bytes. For a request r larger than the minimum, the chosen block B satisfies
B/2<r<=B, hence 0<=B-r<B/2. Requests at or below the minimum are an exception
to the usual half-block bound: a one-byte request with a 32-byte minimum wastes
31 bytes, which is 96.875% of its reserved block.

> Adjacent free blocks can still fail a larger request

Consider a 256-byte arena with eight 32-byte blocks. Fill it, then release
offsets 32 and 64. Those free intervals are adjacent, with 64 free bytes in
total, but neither can merge: the buddy of offset 32 is zero, and the buddy
of offset 64 is 96. Both buddies are still allocated. A 64-byte request fails.
Releasing zero permits the true pair at offsets zero and 32 to merge, making
a 64-byte request succeed at offset zero.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/buddy_allocator_fragmentation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::algorithms::BuddyAllocator arena(256,32);
  std::vector<int> offsets;
  for (int i=0;i<8;++i) offsets.push_back(arena.allocate(32));
  (void)arena.free_trace(offsets[1]);(void)arena.free_trace(offsets[2]);
  const auto fragmented=arena.snapshot();
  const auto failure=arena.allocate_trace(64);
  if (failure.offset!=-1 || fragmented.free_bytes!=64 || fragmented.largest_free_block!=32) return 1;
  const auto release=arena.free_trace(offsets[0]);
  const auto coalesced=arena.snapshot();
  const auto success=arena.allocate_trace(64);
  if (success.offset!=0 || release.merges!=1) return 1;
  std::print("| state | free bytes | largest free block | request | returned offset |\n"
             "| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n"
             "| free offsets 32 and 64 | {} | {} | 64 | {} |\n"
             "| also release offset 0 | {} | {} | 64 | {} |\n\n",
      fragmented.free_bytes,fragmented.largest_free_block,failure.offset,
      coalesced.free_bytes,coalesced.largest_free_block,success.offset);
  std::print("| current offset | order | computed buddy | buddy in that free set |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for (const auto& p:release.probes)
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",p.offset,p.order,p.buddy_offset,p.buddy_free);
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram(65,1100);
  for (const auto& [state,y]:std::vector<std::pair<const dm::algorithms::BuddySnapshot*,double>>{
      {&fragmented,0},{&coalesced,-3.5}}) {
    for (const auto& block:state->blocks) {
      const double left=block.offset/16.0,right=(block.offset+block.size)/16.0;
      dm::graphics::DiagramStroke border;border.color={71,85,105};
      diagram.polygon({{left,y-0.6},{right,y-0.6},{right,y+0.6},{left,y+0.6}},
          block.allocated?dm::RGB{254,226,226}:dm::RGB{220,252,231},border)
          .text({(left+right)/2,y},std::format("{}\n{} B",block.allocated?"live":"free",block.size),15)
          .text({left,y-1},std::format("{}",block.offset),14);
    }
    diagram.text({16,y-1},"256",14);
  }
  diagram.text({8,1.5},"adjacent free intervals [32,64) and [64,96): not buddies",17)
      .text({8,-2},"release zero: [0,64) coalesces, [64,96) stays separate",17)
      .text({8,-5.3},"green = free; red = live; widths are proportional to bytes",16)
      .save_svg("build/buddy_allocator_fragmentation.svg");
  std::print("\nFailed allocation examined {} eligible orders and changed no state.\n",failure.orders_examined);
}
```
